<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		A render-deferred widget draws itself when its timer fires. If its placeholder is gone by
		then, the timer must give up instead of binding a widget that has no DOM.
		1. Click "detach" within 4 seconds. There should be no JS error in the console (F12).
		2. The control below is left alone, so after 4 seconds its selectbox shows up.
	</label>

	<div id="d" renderdefer="4000">
		<selectbox id="sb"/>
	</div>

	<label value="control (never detached):"/>
	<div id="ctrl" renderdefer="4000">
		<selectbox id="sbCtrl"/>
	</div>

	<button id="detach" label="detach" onClick="d.detach()"/>
</zk>
